    "document": {
        "blocks": [
            {
                "id": "b351",
                "type": "front-cover",
                "align": "center",
                "theme": null,
                "expanded": false,
                "src": "data:image/png;base64,",
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b353",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "center",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "",
                "dropCap": null,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b1",
                "type": "title",
                "align": "center",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "Talesmith Language",
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b160",
                "type": "subtitle",
                "align": "center",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "Specification 0.1",
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b159",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "center",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "",
                "dropCap": null,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b2",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "center",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "A web-native document format for paged and web reading.",
                "dropCap": null,
                "cols": 2,
                "alignOverride": true
            },
            {
                "id": "b352",
                "type": "full-page",
                "align": "center",
                "theme": null,
                "expanded": false,
                "text": "Talesmith Language (.tsl)\nBy J.B Crossland\n",
                "hAlign": "center",
                "vAlign": "center",
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b178",
                "type": "toc",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "expanded": false,
                "maxLevel": 3,
                "leader": ".",
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b173",
                "type": "pageheader",
                "align": "center",
                "theme": null,
                "textLeft": "",
                "textCenter": "[Title]-[RunningHeader]",
                "textRight": "",
                "side": "any",
                "expanded": false,
                "cols": 2,
                "text": "[Title]-[RunningHeader]"
            },
            {
                "id": "b354",
                "type": "pagefooter",
                "align": "center",
                "theme": null,
                "textLeft": "tls 0.1",
                "textCenter": "",
                "textRight": "[PageNo]/[PageCount]",
                "side": "any",
                "expanded": false,
                "cols": 2,
                "text": "[PageNo]/[PageCount]"
            },
            {
                "id": "b179",
                "type": "newpage",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b3",
                "type": "h1",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "Purpose and constraints",
                "cols": 2,
                "number": "1"
            },
            {
                "id": "b4",
                "type": "h2",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "The problem",
                "cols": 2,
                "number": "1.1"
            },
            {
                "id": "b165",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "Writers are faced with **disparate** systems and **fractured** processes that distract from the work they need to focus on. The writer should be spending all their time outlining, writing, editing and marketing, not exporting, formatting and debugging why a page header is not visible on page seven or why the page numbers in the table of contents are not updating. The problems are real despite there being a multitude of tools.",
                "dropCap": {
                    "lines": 1,
                    "style": "normal",
                    "characters": 1,
                    "includeLeadingPunctuation": true,
                    "spacingEm": 0.08000000000000000166533453693773481063544750213623046875,
                    "opticalMargin": true,
                    "alignBaseline": true,
                    "uppercase": false,
                    "variant": "default",
                    "capStyle": null
                },
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b167",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "The problem is the editor. Talesmith takes the view that many of the issues derive from it.",
                "dropCap": null,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b168",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "Editors have generally followed the Microsoft Word or Adobe PDF line of thinking, with the web as a secondary output. HTML started out as a metaphor for documents, but this was largely subsumed by application-centric ideas. The document or page was now a web page with colour backgrounds, z-index, dialogs and mechanisms for event-driven development and browser APIs. Although HTML did include additional meta tags like 'article' and 'nav', you can see the tug of war between the page and the web page in the name of these two additions.",
                "dropCap": null,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b169",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "Talesmith understands this as a primary reason for the lack of printer support, and even why @media is better supported than print and why it's all technically generalised as media types. PDF is still used as the most relevant paged media absolute setting, whereas HTML plays with relative and absolute in an entirely different way. Continuous scroll versus paged content has different meaning across HTML and Word.",
                "dropCap": null,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b170",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "What we may be talking about here is a form of WYSIWYG (What you see is what you get), which set a very low bar for that statement. The growth of markdown points to issues with editors: it is a very clear statement against the WYSIWYG, paged vs continuous page, relative vs absolute, formatting vs content issues that we experience as writers. Although sometimes it could purely be a bug that could be fixed, we are tired of not understanding why the next paragraph suddenly changed styling, and having to re-apply a style for the fifth time is mentally exhausting and a large distraction.",
                "dropCap": null,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b171",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "The problem is also the way in which we interpret our <strong>writing</strong> and how we want to present it, as an article or as a book, as defined or as calculable by conditions like screen size. This has made the epub standard a nightmare, and why ePub 3 is such a welcome improvement. ePub 3 effectively does less by itself, and that seems to be the better answer. However, having yet another format, a mixture of HTML and other technologies muddied together to form this electronic reading material, adds to the problem of import, export and the writer's nightmare of the writing-to-publishing pipeline.",
                "dropCap": null,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b172",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "If the editor is the problem, another editor in the same lineage is not the answer. Talesmith's answer is to separate what the writer means from how it looks — the writer says \"this paragraph opens with a three-line drop cap, this page runs a header on the left,\" and the page, or the screen, works out the rest. That separation is Talesmith Language, and the rest of this document specifies it.",
                "dropCap": null,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b6",
                "type": "h2",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "TSL as the distributed format",
                "cols": 2,
                "number": "1.2"
            },
            {
                "id": "b7",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "We have many formats to contend with and their design decisions and capabilities have allowed for the usual pros and cons. For example, Word has had many formats over the decades, RTF is basic, PDF is complex, HTML and markdown are simpler but cannot do what PDF can. However, PDF requires a binary viewer and complex embedded HTML containers. A Google Doc does not reveal its format. All of these are targeted towards specific devices or media. HTML is universal in many senses, and epub chose it for that reason. However, as we have discussed HTML is not capable of storing the requirements for an editor and a document reader. The industry has split these two things and this may be part of the issue. Although it is great being able to import and export, it is only due to limitations that we move from one to another. The hope is that if we dont have complex typography here, we export and get it in the other editor. But this comes at a price. The formats are rarely interchangeble with loss. And to an author, a published file, a reader, even the slightest loss can mean the difference in reader experience, author's wishes, capabilities and so on.",
                "dropCap": null,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b175",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "The answer for Talesmith at least, is to create a single web, desktop, any capability, any media format and therefore there is nothing to lose. By specifying the rules, rendering can be done by CSS/JS and or your render engine. The goal is a single source and distribution format.",
                "dropCap": null,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b10",
                "type": "h2",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "Relationship to HTML, PDF, and typesetting tools",
                "cols": 2,
                "number": "1.3"
            },
            {
                "id": "b11",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "HTML/CSS is the presentation of the web. The Talesmith Language is expressed in JSON format and any JSON serialiser can be used to read and the build a renderer. By default, the TSL lab is a working example JavaScript/HTML/CSS native renderer.\n",
                "dropCap": null,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b25812",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "HTML was first developed as a document for the web and included headings and paragraphs, bullet points and basic formatting like bold and underline. It was far too rudimentary for real document work, and subsequently a tug of war between application development or documents has existed. At the same time, great work was done on the PDF. The two platforms are mainly thought of as continuous flow vs fixed print-ready. The opposites are also basically true, web being not so print-ready and pdf not so flow capable.",
                "dropCap": null,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b25813",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "For a publisher the gap was largely filled by roles, the writer and editor worried about the words, the book designer did the typography and layout, and they often used an editor, paper print out and a DTP tool, importing and exporting whatever was required. The idea of setting up text and exporting it to PDF or ePub became normal. ",
                "dropCap": null,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b25814",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "Talesmith wants to change this for the digital age and remove the historical steps.",
                "dropCap": null,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b25815",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "ePub is HTML constrained and contorted. PDF is print. DTP tools are still the primary connector between author and reader. However, users want to change the font-size and read it on their favourite device. The modern formats are either trying to replicate a book, or replicate video/audio and web design. This is confusing what a digital book should be, with print and other media. It doesn't know what it is.",
                "dropCap": null,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b25816",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "Talesmith is designed to be a digital reading experience, not a showcase for animation or presentation. Talesmith will leave the audio visual experiences to those technologies that do that best. PDF and ePub are moving into an everything for everyone format. Talesmith is for digital books and for the author to published pipeline.",
                "dropCap": null,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b14",
                "type": "h1",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "Document Model",
                "cols": 2,
                "number": "2"
            },
            {
                "id": "b25840",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "The first object requires format and version properties. ",
                "dropCap": null,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b25841",
                "type": "aside",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "All versions 0.1-0.9 are technically version 1 in development. ",
                "icon": "✅",
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b25853",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "",
                "dropCap": null,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b25833",
                "type": "table",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "cells": [
                    [
                        "format",
                        "\"talesmith-lang\" — envelope discriminator"
                    ],
                    [
                        "version",
                        "integer 1 — format version (draft)"
                    ],
                    [
                        "header.theme",
                        "default | serif | dark | compact — reader CSS theme id"
                    ],
                    [
                        "header.readMode",
                        "true | false — replace [Field] tokens in block text when true"
                    ],
                    [
                        "header.allowScrollMode",
                        "true | false — allow continuous scroll layout (default true)"
                    ],
                    [
                        "header.numheadings",
                        "numerals | roman — optional outline style for h1–h3 labels"
                    ]
                ],
                "header": false,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b25839",
                "type": "code",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "{  \n\"format\": \"talesmith-lang\",  \n\"version\": 1,\n\"theme\": \"default\",\n\"readMode\": false,\n\"allowScrollMode\": true,\n\"header\": {    \n  \"page\": {},    \n  \"typography\": {},   \n  \"numbering\": {},\n  \"metadata\" : {},\n  \"mergeFields\" : {}\n  }, \n  \"document\": {\n    \"blocks\": []\n  }\n}",
                "caption": "Top Level TSL Structure",
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b25855",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "",
                "dropCap": null,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b71",
                "type": "h2",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "Header",
                "cols": 2,
                "number": "2.1"
            },
            {
                "id": "b25834",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "The header is mandatory for reader applications, but not for importing or opening a document in an editor as the header can be reconstructed. The document content must always be extractable, even if headers are missing, as the content is always worth recovery.",
                "dropCap": null,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b25854",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "The header elements are discussed below.",
                "dropCap": null,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b25842",
                "type": "h3",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "Page",
                "cols": 2,
                "number": "2.1.1"
            },
            {
                "id": "b25860",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "Outlines the page requirements. Pages are set for exact print size, and a target for screen. ",
                "dropCap": null,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b25858",
                "type": "table",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "cells": [
                    [
                        "formatId",
                        "web | custom | us-novel | us-mass-market | us-business | us-reference | uk-novel | uk-business | uk-reference — preset chosen in Studio"
                    ],
                    [
                        "kind",
                        "web | print — layout mode after resolve"
                    ],
                    [
                        "trimMM",
                        "{ width, height } number (mm) — resolved page size"
                    ],
                    [
                        "trimIn",
                        "{ width, height } number (in) — print/custom only"
                    ],
                    [
                        "marginsMM",
                        "{ top, bottom, outside, gutter } number (mm)"
                    ],
                    [
                        "marginsIn",
                        "same keys (in) — print/custom only"
                    ],
                    [
                        "headerTopMM",
                        "number (mm) — distance from trim to header text"
                    ],
                    [
                        "footerBottomMM",
                        "number (mm) — distance from trim to footer text"
                    ],
                    [
                        "rowGapMM",
                        "number (mm) — gap between header/footer rule and body"
                    ],
                    [
                        "headerRule",
                        "true | false — line above running header"
                    ],
                    [
                        "footerRule",
                        "true | false — line above running footer"
                    ],
                    [
                        "usePrintGutters",
                        "true | false — mirror inside/outside margins on left/right pages"
                    ],
                    [
                        "sidesMM",
                        "{ left, right } each { left, right } (mm) — effective side padding per page side"
                    ],
                    [
                        "bleed",
                        "null — no bleed value in export today"
                    ],
                    [
                        "unusedCustomFormat",
                        "object — saved custom trim/margins when formatId is not custom"
                    ]
                ],
                "header": false,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b25844",
                "type": "h3",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "Typography",
                "cols": 2,
                "number": "2.1.2"
            },
            {
                "id": "b25861",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "Resolved defaults for body text; fontFamily is the CSS stack applied at render time.",
                "dropCap": null,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b25862",
                "type": "table",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "cells": [
                    [
                        "presetId",
                        "string — style preset id or custom (provenance only)"
                    ],
                    [
                        "fontId",
                        "book-serif | georgia | times | palatino | garamond | baskerville | sans | courier"
                    ],
                    [
                        "fontFamily",
                        "string — resolved CSS font stack for fontId"
                    ],
                    [
                        "sizePt",
                        "number 6–36 — body size in points"
                    ],
                    [
                        "lineHeight",
                        "number 1–3 — unitless line height"
                    ],
                    [
                        "paragraphAlign",
                        "left | center | right | justify — default paragraph alignment"
                    ],
                    [
                        "paragraphIndentIn",
                        "number 0–2 — first-line indent (inches)"
                    ],
                    [
                        "paragraphSpacingPt",
                        "number 0–36 — space after paragraph (points)"
                    ],
                    [
                        "hyphenation",
                        "true | false — CSS hyphenation on body text"
                    ]
                ],
                "header": false,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b25846",
                "type": "h3",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "Numbering",
                "cols": 2,
                "number": "2.1.3"
            },
            {
                "id": "b25863",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "Controls printed page numbers and which physical sheet counts as page one.",
                "dropCap": null,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b25864",
                "type": "table",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "cells": [
                    [
                        "startPage",
                        "integer ≥ 1 — number shown on the first numbered sheet"
                    ],
                    [
                        "pageOffsetStart",
                        "integer ≥ 0 — unnumbered front-matter sheets before numbering"
                    ],
                    [
                        "firstPhysicalPageSide",
                        "left — first physical page is a left (verso) page"
                    ]
                ],
                "header": false,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b25848",
                "type": "h3",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "Metadata",
                "cols": 2,
                "number": "2.1.4"
            },
            {
                "id": "b25865",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "Document fields and publish context; fields round-trip with the editor customFields list.",
                "dropCap": null,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b25866",
                "type": "table",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "cells": [
                    [
                        "fields",
                        "array of { name, value } string — author-defined merge fields"
                    ],
                    [
                        "title",
                        "string — optional publish title"
                    ],
                    [
                        "category",
                        "{ id, name } — optional publish category"
                    ]
                ],
                "header": false,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b25850",
                "type": "h3",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "MergeFields",
                "cols": 2,
                "number": "2.1.5"
            },
            {
                "id": "b25852",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "Resolved map for [Field] substitution when readMode is true; computed page tokens are filled at render time and are not stored in fields.",
                "dropCap": null,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b25867",
                "type": "table",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "cells": [
                    [
                        "version",
                        "number — merge map version (1 in Studio export; 0.1 when synthesised by the player)"
                    ],
                    [
                        "fields",
                        "array of { name, value, used } — declared and discovered tokens"
                    ],
                    [
                        "fields[].name",
                        "string matching [A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9 _.-]* — display name without brackets"
                    ],
                    [
                        "fields[].value",
                        "string — substituted text (may be empty)"
                    ],
                    [
                        "fields[].used",
                        "true | false — token appears somewhere in document.blocks"
                    ],
                    [
                        "values",
                        "object — keys are normalised lowercase names; values are strings for substitution"
                    ],
                    [
                        "computed tokens",
                        "[PageNo] [PageCount] [RunningHeader] [Title] [WordCount] [Lines] [Date] [Time] [AuthorLastName] … — filled at render; aliases like [Page] and [RunningHead] map to the same keys"
                    ]
                ],
                "header": false,
                "cols": 2
            },
            {
                "id": "b72",
                "type": "h2",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "text": "Document",
                "cols": 2,
                "number": "2.2"
            },
            {
                "id": "b25868",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "cols": 2,
                "text": "The document object holds the block list and, in the editor, settings that export into header on publish. Players read header plus document.blocks; missing header values may be synthesised from document settings.",
                "dropCap": null
            },
            {
                "id": "b25869",
                "type": "h3",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "cols": 2,
                "text": "Document object",
                "number": "2.2.1"
            },
            {
                "id": "b25870",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "cols": 2,
                "text": "Top-level document keys besides blocks (also listed under §2.1 when resolved into header).",
                "dropCap": null
            },
            {
                "id": "b25871",
                "type": "table",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "cols": 2,
                "cells": [
                    [
                        "blocks",
                        "array — ordered block objects (required)"
                    ],
                    [
                        "pageFormat",
                        "web | custom | us-novel | us-mass-market | us-business | us-reference | uk-novel | uk-business | uk-reference"
                    ],
                    [
                        "typography",
                        "object — fontId, sizePt, lineHeight, paragraphAlign, paragraphIndentIn, paragraphSpacingPt, presetId"
                    ],
                    [
                        "customFormat",
                        "object { trimIn, marginsIn } — active when pageFormat is custom"
                    ],
                    [
                        "customFields",
                        "array of { name, value } — author fields; see §2.1.4"
                    ],
                    [
                        "usePrintGutters",
                        "true | false"
                    ],
                    [
                        "hyphenation",
                        "true | false"
                    ],
                    [
                        "theme",
                        "default | serif | dark | compact"
                    ],
                    [
                        "startPage",
                        "integer ≥ 1"
                    ],
                    [
                        "pageOffsetStart",
                        "integer ≥ 0"
                    ],
                    [
                        "numheadings",
                        "numerals | roman — optional outline numbering for h1–h3"
                    ],
                    [
                        "allowScrollMode",
                        "true | false"
                    ]
                ],
                "header": false
            },
            {
                "id": "b25872",
                "type": "h3",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "cols": 2,
                "text": "Common block properties",
                "number": "2.2.2"
            },
            {
                "id": "b25873",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "cols": 2,
                "text": "Every block includes these; unknown type loads as paragraph in Studio.",
                "dropCap": null
            },
            {
                "id": "b25874",
                "type": "table",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "cols": 2,
                "cells": [
                    [
                        "id",
                        "string — stable id (e.g. b12), preserved on load"
                    ],
                    [
                        "type",
                        "string — block type id (see §2.2.3)"
                    ],
                    [
                        "align",
                        "left | center | right | justify — invalid values become left"
                    ],
                    [
                        "cols",
                        "1 | 2 — column span; newpage is always full width"
                    ],
                    [
                        "theme",
                        "null | default | serif | dark | compact — optional block theme override"
                    ],
                    [
                        "text (many types)",
                        "string — inline HTML subset, not plain text; may contain [Field] tokens"
                    ]
                ],
                "header": false
            },
            {
                "id": "b25875",
                "type": "h3",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "cols": 2,
                "text": "Block types",
                "number": "2.2.3"
            },
            {
                "id": "b25876",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "cols": 2,
                "text": "Type-specific fields in addition to §2.2.2; extra keys are preserved for round-trip.",
                "dropCap": null
            },
            {
                "id": "b25877",
                "type": "table",
                "align": "left",
                "theme": null,
                "cols": 2,
                "cells": [
                    [
                        "title",
                        "text"
                    ],
                    [
                        "subtitle",
                        "text"
                    ],
                    [
                        "paragraph",
                        "text; dropCap object|null; alignOverride true — block align wins over typography"
                    ],
                    [
                        "h1 | h2 | h3",
                        "text; number string|null — outline label (e.g. 2.1)"
                    ],
                    [
                        "quote",
                        "text"
                    ],
                    [
                        "code",
                        "text (plain in player); caption string"
                    ],
                    [
                        "bullet",
                        "text; bulletStyle disc | circle | square | dash | number | lower-alpha | upper-alpha"
                    ],
                    [
                        "todo",
                        "text; checked true | false"
                    ],
                    [
                        "aside",
                        "text; icon string — short prefix, default light-bulb emoji"
                    ],
                    [
                        "divider",
                        "— no extra fields"
                    ],
                    [
                        "newpage",
                        "— page break; cols ignored"
                    ],
                    [
                        "image",
                        "src string (URL or data: URI); caption string; width integer 10–100 (percent)"
                    ],
                    [
                        "table",
                        "cells string[][]; header true | false"
                    ],
                    [
                        "toc",
                        "expanded boolean; maxLevel integer 1–3; leader string (≤4 chars, default \".\")"
                    ],
                    [
                        "image-index",
                        "expanded boolean; leader string; title string"
                    ],
                    [
                        "full-page",
                        "text; hAlign left | center | right; vAlign top | center | bottom; expanded boolean"
                    ],
                    [
                        "paywall",
                        "text; roles string[] — node role ids; expanded boolean"
                    ],
                    [
                        "front-cover",
                        "src string; expanded boolean — full-bleed cover image"
                    ],
                    [
                        "pageheader | pagefooter",
                        "textLeft, textCenter, textRight strings; side any | left | right; expanded boolean"
                    ],
                    [
                        "document",
                        "documentId string|null; title string; expanded boolean — embed reference, flattened on publish"
                    ],
                    [
                        "manuscript-title",
                        "kind novel | short-story | poem; expanded boolean; title, byline, authorInfo, wordCount, linesCount, contact strings"
                    ],
                    [
                        "script-scene",
                        "text; showSceneNumbers boolean; sceneNumberLeft, sceneNumberRight digit strings (≤4)"
                    ],
                    [
                        "script-action | script-dialogue | script-parenthetical | script-transition | script-shot",
                        "text"
                    ],
                    [
                        "script-character",
                        "text — character name (uppercase in screenplay layout)"
                    ],
                    [
                        "stage-scene | stage-action | stage-direction",
                        "text"
                    ],
                    [
                        "stage-speech",
                        "character string; text string"
                    ],
                    [
                        "mathml",
                        "source string (MathML or LaTeX); display boolean — block vs inline; sourceExpanded boolean (editor UI)"
                    ]
                ],
                "header": false
            }
        ]
    }
}
